maria (DevEx): Support reported a Cloudflare Worker quickstart copied Node `require()` and got "TypeError: mod.default is undefined". They also saw repeated 401 retries. Can we clarify samples + retry behavior?

sam (SDK): Short answer: use ESM snippets for edge. Example: 
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/inference';
const c = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: Deno.env.get('REDWOOD_KEY') });

For Node CJS only: 
const mod = require('@redwood/inference');
const RedwoodClient = mod?.default ?? mod?.RedwoodClient ?? mod;

Also: do not retry on 401/403 by default.

oj (Runtime): Edge timer polyfills can make backoffs look instant. We should lower retry attempts in edge builds and validate auth before scheduling retries.

docs-bot: Opening docs task: standardize quickstarts per runtime (node/worker/vite), add CJS appendix, TS note (esModuleInterop), and auth-retry guidance.

maria (DevEx): Great. I'll add a short support checklist: runtime, bundler, snippet used, token source. Thanks!
